WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.900
(bold rock music)

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.860
- My ultimate goal is just
to have my name up there

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.490
with my dad's name when they're picking

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.170
some of the best drivers in the industry

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.560
to work on a big car show.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.510
You know, I don't wanna
be the best woman driver,

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:17.010
the best Black woman driver,
I wanna be the best driver.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.277
I mean--
- One of the best drivers.

00:00:18.277 --> 00:00:20.200
- Okay.
- Don't get too cocky,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.451
'cause then I ain't gonna be able to work.

00:00:22.451 --> 00:00:24.963
- Ah, ha, ha, ha, you're so funny.

00:00:24.963 --> 00:00:28.130
(car engines revving)

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.140
My name is Brionna
Lynch, I'm 21 years old,

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.010
and I've been a stunt
driver for 4 1/2 years.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.420
- My name is Jalil Jay Lynch, I'm her dad

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.170
and I've been in the
business for 27 years.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.770
- All the dangerous stuff
that the cars are doing

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:46.200
in the movies, all the exciting stuff?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.730
We do that and not the actors.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.500
So a couple of the films
that I've worked on

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.890
are Black Panther, Proud
Mary, Fast and Furious 8,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.050
Beyonce's music video
Formation, and Creed,

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.390
and that's me and my dad right there.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.700
- [Jalil] I got started in the
business doing New Jack City.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.030
I've done all the Fast and
Furious series since number four.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.870
In Jumanji, I'm one of the
guys up there on the bike.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.980
Yep, that's me right there.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.439
- So cool.
- 'Cause I am the coolest--

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:10.560
- 12 o'clocking it.
- Dad ever.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.960
- When my dad and I are working together,

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.050
we actually like to help
each other set the cars up,

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.420
so when I have to do something

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.030
like sliding around the corner,

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.720
my dad is right there with
me trying to make sure

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.410
that everything is set up, so I think

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.831
that's what makes my
dad and I really unique.

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:24.664
(tires squealing)

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.150
I got into stunt driving
because of my dad.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:33.160
He taught me how to ride
when I was three years old,

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.080
he's been teaching me my entire life.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.900
He's so good at what he does

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.380
and so respected in this industry,

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.730
so since I started stunt-driving
he has been my motivator,

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.190
my coach, my teacher.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:48.638
He's everything but my
accountant, pretty much.

00:01:48.638 --> 00:01:50.236
That sounds like fun.

00:01:50.236 --> 00:01:51.069
- Bang.

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.800
One of the things that I had learned

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.880
by riding with her all the time

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.920
was that she was able
to handle the pressure.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.590
Three, two, one, action.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.660
As much as people don't believe

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.550
that you're inside a
car when they explode,

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.670
people are in those
vehicles, so it's a lot

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.970
to let your kid go and be in danger.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.560
I guess part of being a
parent and part of being

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.900
in the stunt business,
we do as much as we can

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.510
to keep her as safe as
possible and then after that

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.595
you wish for the best.

00:02:22.595 --> 00:02:25.172
(tires squealing)

00:02:25.172 --> 00:02:26.505
Good job, kiddo.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.460
- I love that I get to share
stunt driving with my dad.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:33.640
I think that's a really cool
bond that the two of us have.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.270
My dad and I have always been very close.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.840
He's very supportive of
me chasing down this dream

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.990
that I have and, if you
wanna be good at something,

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.320
you have to put the time in.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.770
It's important for you to enjoy your life

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.070
and to actually love what you're doing.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.635
That's the biggest picture
at the end of the day.

00:02:47.635 --> 00:02:50.218
(upbeat music)

